<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Metrostav posts Q1 CZK 22 MLN net.</title>
<headline>Czech Metrostav posts Q1 CZK 22 MLN net.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for three-month period ending March 31</p>
<p>(in millions of crowns).</p>
<p>				   1997			1996</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit	     29.330		    20.131</p>
<p> After tax profit	   22.199		    16.237</p>
<p> operating profit	   28.717		    15.501</p>
<p> writeoffs		    28.029		    26.060</p>
<p>sales of own goods</p>
<p> and services	    1,207.398		 1,072.753</p>
<p> Basic capital assets    658.889		   508.889</p>
<p> Assets		    2,899.129		 2,779.806</p>
<p>NOTE: The company's full name is Metrostav a.s.. It is one of the largest Czech building companies and is quoted on the PX50 index of the Prague Stock Exchange. Metrostav said it would pay a gross dividend on 1996 profits of 70 crowns, the same as in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Robin Shepherd, Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
